From b9a228bd11e331061f0c02ca28182dd542e925f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 20:27:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06956/11362] Task 8: fix PTRM generation/trained-model wiring
 bug; multi-seed LOO gate fails, retire TRM-as-generator (REQ-ARC-PTRM-5600)

generate_trajectories previously ignored the trained PTRMActionSequenceGenerator
entirely, seeding every trajectory from the untrained _base_action_logits
frequency heuristic. _train_proxy_model genuinely trained the model via real
backprop and a real checkpoint, but the weights were never consulted at
generation time. Fixed by threading an optional model through
generate_trajectories -> _recursion_metrics -> run_experiment_5574.

Also found and disclosed: the checked-in exp5574 artifact (committed in
70c857a69, an unrelated-titled commit) contains fields the code in that same
commit cannot compute -- it could not have been produced by the code it
shipped with. Preserved unmodified per never-prune discipline; flagged as
untrustworthy pending investigation.

Built the multi-seed (10 seeds x 5 games), pre-registered leave-one-game-out
gate the wiring fix unblocks (exp5600), reusing v3's held-out game set and
Wilcoxon methodology. Real run: gate FAILS -- only ft09 (1 of 5) clears both
significance and majority-baseline bars, below the required majority of 3.
Per known-issues.md task 8's retire_if_same_verdict: true, the TRM-as-
generator line for ARC-AGI-3 is retired.

results/experiment_5600_ptrm_loo_gate.json was already committed under an
unrelated conductor commit (9063c7f5b) via its own git-add-everything
behavior; content is byte-identical to the real run and not re-added here.

